---
const pageTitle = 'About Me';
const identity = {
	name: 'David',
	role: 'Web Developer',
	bio: 'I am a web developer with a passion',
	hobbies: ['coding', 'reading', 'gaming']
}
const skills = ["HTML", "CSS", "JavaScript",  "Astro", "Writing Docs"];


---

<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<meta charset="utf-8" />
		<link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
		<link rel="icon" href="/favicon.ico" />
		<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
		<meta name="generator" content={Astro.generator} />
		<title>{pageTitle}</title>
		<link rel="stylesheet" href="../src/output.css" />
	</head>
	<body>
 <header>
			<nav class="px-4">
        <ul>
          <li><a href="/">Home</a></li>
          <li><a href="/blog">Blog</a></li>
			    <li><a href="/about">About</a></li>

        </ul>
			
		</nav>
		</header>
    <main class="container p-10">
		<h1>{pageTitle}</h1>
    <small>...and my new blog</small>
    <p>I'm working through Astro's Tutorial to build this site. I'm also using  a hybrid  Pico/Tailwind CSS approach.</p>
		 <p>Here are a few things about me</p>
		 	<ul>
				<li><strong>Name:</strong> {identity.name}</li>
				<li><strong>Role:</strong> {identity.role}</li>
				<li><strong>Bio:</strong> {identity.bio}</li>
				<li><strong>Hobbies:</strong> {identity.hobbies.join(', ')}</li>
			</ul>
			<p>And some of my skills are:</p>
			
			<ul>
				{skills.map((skill) => (
				<li>{skill}</li>))}
				</ul>
    </main>
	</body>
</html>
